From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] build: a release may name itself in the build number

`ro.build.display.id` is the line Settings shows as 「版本号」 / Build number,
and on this port it reads `OC dev-keys`: the `BUILD_ID` the tree ships with and
the key tag. Nothing in the image says which release it is, so a reader filing
a problem cannot say what they have, and the `builde10271833` inside the
fingerprint is not a version anyone can read out (docs/open-items.md).

Setting `BUILD_DISPLAY_ID` in the environment does not reach it, which is what
this patch is for. 8.1 assigns the variable with `:=` in both branches of
`core/Makefile`, unconditionally, so whatever the environment holds is
overwritten before `tools/buildinfo.sh` reads it back out. Measured rather than
assumed: V91 was first built with `BUILD_DISPLAY_ID="Readom V91"` exported to
kati beside `BUILD_DATETIME` and `BUILD_NUMBER`, and the image's build.prop
came out `ro.build.display.id=OC dev-keys` all the same. Soong is not what
dropped it -- `build/soong/ui/build/config.go` unsets a named list of fifteen
variables and this is not one of them.

The guard is the one later AOSP carries in `version_defaults.mk`: fill the
variable in only when it is empty. Both assignments, their condition and their
comments are untouched; they are skipped only when there is already an answer,
so a build that passes nothing gets exactly what it got before, in every
variant.

Nothing else reads `BUILD_DISPLAY_ID`. It reaches `build.prop` through
`buildinfo.sh` and goes nowhere near `BUILD_ID`, `BUILD_NUMBER`, the
fingerprint or `build_desc`, so two builds that differ only in this differ in
that single line of build.prop.

--- a/core/Makefile
+++ b/core/Makefile
@@ -212,19 +212,26 @@
     $(PRODUCTS.$(INTERNAL_PRODUCT).PRODUCT_OEM_PROPERTIES))
 
 # Display parameters shown under Settings -> About Phone
-ifeq ($(TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT),user)
-  # User builds should show:
-  # release build number or branch.buld_number non-release builds
+# PW3: only when the build did not bring one of its own. Later AOSP guards
+# these assignments the same way, in version_defaults.mk; 8.1 assigns with :=
+# over whatever the environment holds, so a release had no way to name itself
+# in the one line Settings shows as the build number. A build that passes
+# nothing gets exactly what it got before, in every variant.
+ifeq (,$(strip $(BUILD_DISPLAY_ID)))
+  ifeq ($(TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT),user)
+    # User builds should show:
+    # release build number or branch.buld_number non-release builds
 
-  # Dev. branches should have DISPLAY_BUILD_NUMBER set
-  ifeq (true,$(DISPLAY_BUILD_NUMBER))
-    BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(BUILD_ID).$(BUILD_NUMBER_FROM_FILE) $(BUILD_KEYS)
+    # Dev. branches should have DISPLAY_BUILD_NUMBER set
+    ifeq (true,$(DISPLAY_BUILD_NUMBER))
+      BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(BUILD_ID).$(BUILD_NUMBER_FROM_FILE) $(BUILD_KEYS)
+    else
+      BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(BUILD_ID) $(BUILD_KEYS)
+    endif
   else
-    BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(BUILD_ID) $(BUILD_KEYS)
+    # Non-user builds should show detailed build information
+    BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(build_desc)
   endif
-else
-  # Non-user builds should show detailed build information
-  BUILD_DISPLAY_ID := $(build_desc)
 endif
 
